WEBVTT

00:00:01.100 --> 00:00:08.176
Narrator: Four friends enter a candlelit parlor: Ada, Ben, Cora, and Dax. This is one possible run, with two

00:00:08.176 --> 00:00:11.715
Narrator: survivors. The ending shown is a proposal, still undecided.

00:00:12.035 --> 00:00:17.422
Medium: Four living witnesses. Four seals. Bring them to this table, and her inheritance will open.

00:00:17.742 --> 00:00:25.589
Narrator: The medium believes she is helping. Cora draws the healer. Dax secretly serves the Tory husband: one

00:00:25.589 --> 00:00:27.897
Narrator: misleading suggestion, no physical interference.

00:00:28.217 --> 00:00:36.401
Ghost: I hid messages for the revolution. They murdered my four children. They burned our home. Will you

00:00:36.401 --> 00:00:38.808
Ghost: help me open it again?

00:00:41.808 --> 00:00:48.631
Narrator: Four tutorial cards are honestly shuffled. One is Veiled. Ada draws it by chance. She is blind from

00:00:48.631 --> 00:00:52.422
Narrator: now through her ending, if she survives. Nobody is protected.

00:00:52.742 --> 00:00:58.081
Medium: Now name five hidden symbols in a row. Every card goes back. Every draw is shuffled.

00:00:58.401 --> 00:01:04.223
Narrator: Five correct guesses would win. The chance is one in three thousand, one hundred and twenty-five.

00:01:04.223 --> 00:01:06.406
Narrator: Here, the first guess is wrong.

00:01:06.726 --> 00:01:10.187
Ghost: An offering. A curse. Or one of you.

00:01:10.737 --> 00:01:16.310
Narrator: They keep their four offerings and choose a hearing curse for Ben. His world grows quiet.

00:01:19.080 --> 00:01:25.249
Narrator: In the study, a paper grille hides four letters. Dax suggests turning it sideways. They follow him,

00:01:25.249 --> 00:01:27.064
Narrator: and submit the wrong word.

00:01:27.384 --> 00:01:29.626
Medium: You may still pass. Choose the price.

00:01:29.946 --> 00:01:36.169
Narrator: Cora takes silence. Then she spends her healer token on Ben. He can hear again; she cannot speak.

00:01:36.169 --> 00:01:39.972
Narrator: The medium reveals the answer: BELL. Their first seal is earned.

00:01:40.292 --> 00:01:46.956
Ghost: Smoke took my daughter’s sight. She could not find the door before the fire took her.

00:01:47.506 --> 00:01:52.552
Narrator: Ada understands her blindfold differently now. Each curse remembers a child.

00:01:55.322 --> 00:01:57.032
Ghost: Three. One. Four.

00:01:57.582 --> 00:02:03.775
Narrator: The voice comes from the cold hearth now, without the medium translating. Ada listens. Ben mixes up

00:02:03.775 --> 00:02:08.511
Narrator: the last two numbers. They could ask for a replay; instead, they commit.

00:02:08.831 --> 00:02:14.811
Narrator: Another failure. Ben chooses no hands. No bindings: he simply leaves the objects to his friends.

00:02:14.811 --> 00:02:18.175
Narrator: They receive the second seal and a small drum.

00:02:18.495 --> 00:02:25.574
Ghost: A blow stole my boy’s hearing. He never heard the call to escape the burning house.

00:02:28.574 --> 00:02:34.077
Narrator: Cloth. Cold beads. A ridged star, somewhere inside. Then, with their permission, something briefly

00:02:34.077 --> 00:02:38.793
Narrator: touches Cora’s hand. She jumps, laughs, and pulls out the wrong shape.

00:02:39.113 --> 00:02:44.592
Narrator: Dax volunteers as payment. They are saving offerings for a prize they barely understand. The

00:02:44.592 --> 00:02:50.802
Narrator: collectors lead him out. His clues stay with the group. This is their choice, not a required

00:02:50.802 --> 00:02:51.167
Narrator: removal.

00:02:51.487 --> 00:02:59.322
Ghost: My child’s hands were bound. The door would not open. Dax, your place is ready.

00:02:59.872 --> 00:03:05.630
Narrator: Dax receives his own ending, then returns to the party. Three remain with the third seal.

00:03:08.400 --> 00:03:12.751
Medium: Four tiles. Four words. Speak them, or tap the pattern if your voice is gone.

00:03:13.071 --> 00:03:19.575
Narrator: Ada feels the raised dots. Cora taps. Ben tries to order the words, but their answer comes out

00:03:19.575 --> 00:03:24.635
Narrator: backward. Ben volunteers to pay. The collectors take him, and leave the fourth seal.

00:03:24.955 --> 00:03:34.087
Ghost: They covered my child’s mouth so no alarm could be raised. He never breathed again. Open the house

00:03:34.087 --> 00:03:34.594
Ghost: again.

00:03:35.144 --> 00:03:41.514
Narrator: Now Ada and Cora remain: one blind, one silent. Chance and their choices brought them here.

00:03:41.514 --> 00:03:45.494
Narrator: Successful puzzles or different payments could have left more survivors.

00:03:48.264 --> 00:03:49.782
Ghost: Offer ... yours.

00:03:50.332 --> 00:03:56.111
Medium: The slate says the same thing. But these are your names. Ben and Dax are already marked. Ada. Cora.

00:03:56.111 --> 00:03:57.631
Medium: Your places are still empty.

00:03:57.951 --> 00:04:03.871
Narrator: The medium finally understands. She was never an accomplice. The house has been keeping a family

00:04:03.871 --> 00:04:09.791
Narrator: register, not a treasure map. No moving board is needed; the Ouija remains optional and deferred.

00:04:10.111 --> 00:04:15.026
Medium: Every seal bound a name to this house. We paid for passage. We never bought freedom.

00:04:17.796 --> 00:04:23.321
Ghost: Take what I have saved for you. Or return what you have taken from me.

00:04:23.871 --> 00:04:30.118
Narrator: Cora points to the chest. Ada says yes. The medium opens it. Either story choice completes the

00:04:30.118 --> 00:04:33.058
Narrator: bargain. Their names fill the last two places.

00:04:33.378 --> 00:04:36.728
Medium: Ada. Cora. The inheritance is a place in her family.

00:04:37.048 --> 00:04:42.262
Ghost: Those I took are already here. The rest of you ... are mine.

00:04:45.262 --> 00:04:50.953
Narrator: Four answers rise from the dark. Some sound like children. One sounds almost like Ada.

00:04:51.273 --> 00:04:53.448
Echo: Mother. Mother. Mother. Mother.

00:04:53.768 --> 00:04:57.064
Ghost: Every door you opened made a place for you.

00:04:57.614 --> 00:05:03.832
Narrator: Ada feels her name token turn in her hand. She needs no glimpse of the ghost to understand. They

00:05:03.832 --> 00:05:07.104
Narrator: helped the mother reclaim her family. The price was them.

00:05:07.424 --> 00:05:11.384
Medium: The game is over. You can remove the blindfold now. Come back to the light.

00:05:11.704 --> 00:05:17.286
Narrator: Two reached this ending; neither escaped the fictional bargain. Did they become her children, or

00:05:17.286 --> 00:05:21.008
Narrator: something she owns? That ending is still the captain’s choice.